    "title": "Texas vs. Tennessee odds update: Prediction markets agree on the winner and disagree on everything else - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Mac Douglass ,\n1 days ago Every prediction market in the country has settled on the same number for Saturday’s noon kickoff at Neyland Stadium: No. 1 Texas is a 64–65% favorite over No. 14 Tennessee, and the Dimers predictor lands in the same place at 65%. That is where the agreement ends. Polymarket and Novig have pulled the spread in to Texas -4.5; Kalshi still anchors at 5.5. Polymarket and Novig lean under; Kalshi’s total sits at a dead-even 50%. And on the team totals, Polymarket has Tennessee at 19.5 while Kalshi has the Vols at 26.5—a full touchdown apart on the same team in the same game. Read full article",
    "summary": "1 days ago Every prediction market in the country has settled on the same number for Saturday’s noon kickoff at Neyland Stadium: No. 14 Tennessee, and the Dimers predictor lands in the same place at 65%. Polymarket and Novig have pulled the spread in to Texas -4.5; Kalshi still anchors at 5.5. Polymarket and Novig lean under; Kalshi’s total sits at a dead-even 50%. And on the team totals, Polymarket has Tennessee at 19.5 while Kalshi has the Vols at 26.5—a full touchdown apart on the same team in the same game.",
